@startuml GP20_Process_Flow
' GP-20 · Solution & Cost Architect — skill process flow
' Architecture: one workflow, pluggable model packs.
'
' Notation follows the NSC "RFP Engagement with AI" convention:
' human task / AI agent task / deterministic tool / offering model / decision
'
' Render:
'   plantuml -tsvg process_flow.puml
'   rsvg-convert -w 2600 -a --background-color=white GP20_Process_Flow.svg -o GP20_Process_Flow.png
'
' NOTES FOR ANYONE EDITING THIS FILE
'  * The name on the opening directive names the OUTPUT file, not the source
'    file. Never write that directive again inside a comment — PlantUML reads
'    it even here and starts a second, empty diagram.
'  * A <size:n> tag must open and close on the same physical line, or
'    PlantUML emits the literal closing tag into the diagram.
'  * `backward:` inside a repeat loop is unsupported on 1.2020.02 — use while/endwhile.
'  * Avoid angle brackets in label text; PlantUML reads them as creole tags.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowColor #46586B
skinparam ArrowFontColor #46586B
skinparam ArrowFontSize 12
skinparam TitleFontSize 18
skinparam TitleFontColor #1F3556

skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #DCE7EF
  BorderColor #2E6E8E
  BorderThickness 1.2
  FontColor #1F3556
  FontSize 13
  DiamondBackgroundColor #FDF3E4
  DiamondBorderColor #C8791A
  DiamondFontColor #7A4A0C
  DiamondFontSize 12
  StartColor #1F3556
  EndColor #1F3556
  BarColor #2E6E8E
}

skinparam swimlane {
  BorderColor #9FB3C4
  BorderThickness 1.4
  TitleFontSize 15
}

skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FDF3E4
  BorderColor #C8791A
  FontColor #5C3A0A
  FontSize 11
}

title GP-20 · Solution & Cost Architect — process flow

|#F4F7FA|<color:#1F3556>SOLUTION SHAPER</color>|
start
#F2F5F8:RFP, ITT or tender arrives;
#F2F5F8:Supply the document, plus any
annex, schedule or rate card held;
note right
  .docx, .xlsx or
  meeting notes
end note

|#E4EDF4|<color:#1F3556>GP-20 SKILL  (Claude)</color>|
:Read every input in full
before extracting anything;

|#EAF3EC|<color:#1F3556>SKILL CORE  ·  offering-agnostic</color>|
#E3F0E7:**read_docx.py**  ·  **openpyxl**
<size:11>stdlib reader — no pip, no network</size>;

|#E4EDF4|<color:#1F3556>GP-20 SKILL  (Claude)</color>|
:Identify the offering the
tender is actually asking for;

|#EAF3EC|<color:#1F3556>SKILL CORE  ·  offering-agnostic</color>|
#E3F0E7:**registry.py**   list  ·  detect  ·  describe
<size:11>packs discovered from the models folder — core is never edited</size>;

|#E4EDF4|<color:#1F3556>GP-20 SKILL  (Claude)</color>|
if (Does an installed pack\ncover this offering?) then (**yes**)
else (no)
  #FDF3E4:State plainly that no cost model
  exists, and describe what a pack
  would need to cover it;
  note right
    **No pack, no price.**
    An improvised number is
    worse than an honest gap.
  end note
  stop
endif

:State which pack was chosen,
and why, before going further;

if (Does the tender span\nmore than one offering?) then (**yes**)
  #FDF3E4:Run each pack separately, then assign
  ownership of the service desk — price it with
  the <b>service-desk</b> pack, and set
  **service_desk: false** on the other pack;
  note right
    **managed-lan** and **daas** each embed a
    simplified desk, because a managed
    service without one is not a service.
    Without this step the desk is
    priced twice.
  end note
else (no)
endif

|#EAF3EC|<color:#1F3556>SKILL CORE  ·  offering-agnostic</color>|
#E3F0E7:**registry.py describe**
<size:11>parameter schema · declared gaps · price-material defaults</size>;

|#E4EDF4|<color:#1F3556>GP-20 SKILL  (Claude)</color>|
:Extract parameters and
tag the source of every value
<size:11>rfp · user · derived · default</size>;
note right
  Annex beats prose: a table
  totalling 101 overrides
  "approximately 100"
end note
:Present the extraction table
with section-level citations;

if (Gaps the pack declares\nas price-material?) then (**yes**)
  :**AskUserQuestion**
  <size:11>every option states its commercial consequence</size>;

  |#F4F7FA|<color:#1F3556>SOLUTION SHAPER</color>|
  #F2F5F8:Decide — coverage window, SLA tier,
  language set, refresh cycle, migration ramp;

  |#E4EDF4|<color:#1F3556>GP-20 SKILL  (Claude)</color>|
else (no)
endif

:Write **params.json**
<size:11>with a _sources map, so provenance survives the hand-off</size>;

|#EAF3EC|<color:#1F3556>SKILL CORE  ·  offering-agnostic</color>|
#E3F0E7:**run_estimate.py --pack KEY**
<size:11>the single entry point — validates, dispatches, never prices</size>;

|#F6EFF6|<color:#1F3556>MODEL PACKS  ·  offering-specific</color>|
#EDE0EE:**pack.estimate(params)**
<size:11>rates.py · sizing · coverage floor · year_profile</size>;
note right
  **Installed packs**
  ====
  <b>managed-lan</b>  —  labour-led; geographic coverage floor
  <b>daas</b>  —  capital-led; the refresh cycle dominates
  <b>service-desk</b>  —  language coverage floor
  <b>iaas-compute</b>  —  consumption-led; ramped year profile
  ----
  A new offering is a new folder.
  Nothing in the core changes.
end note

|#EAF3EC|<color:#1F3556>SKILL CORE  ·  offering-agnostic</color>|
#E3F0E7:**contract.verify(result)**
<size:11>shape · provenance tags · unflagged defaults · TCV reconciliation</size>;

if (Does the result\nmeet the contract?) then (**yes**)
else (no)
  #FDF3E4:Report the violation and stop.
  Do not patch around it;
  stop
endif

#E3F0E7:**result.json**
<size:11>estimate · assumption register · review flags</size>;

|#E4EDF4|<color:#1F3556>GP-20 SKILL  (Claude)</color>|
:Present solution shape, service
commitments, transition, run
resources by role and location, TCV;
#FDF3E4:Surface **run.insight**
<size:11>the pack's architectural observation — what actually sets the price</size>;
:List **review_flags**
<size:11>price-material defaults still awaiting confirmation</size>;

|#F4F7FA|<color:#1F3556>SOLUTION SHAPER</color>|
while (Run a sensitivity?) is (**yes**)
  #F2F5F8:Name one parameter to change
  <size:11>coverage · SLA tier · languages · refresh · ramp · term</size>;

  |#E4EDF4|<color:#1F3556>GP-20 SKILL  (Claude)</color>|
  :Rewrite **params.json**;

  |#EAF3EC|<color:#1F3556>SKILL CORE  ·  offering-agnostic</color>|
  #E3F0E7:**run_estimate.py** re-run;

  |#E4EDF4|<color:#1F3556>GP-20 SKILL  (Claude)</color>|
  #FDF3E4:Present the delta against
  the named scenario;

  |#F4F7FA|<color:#1F3556>SOLUTION SHAPER</color>|
endwhile (no)

#F2F5F8:Choose which scenario to price;

|#E4EDF4|<color:#1F3556>GP-20 SKILL  (Claude)</color>|
:Confirm the named scenario,
then generate artefacts;
note right
  Never assume the baseline.
  The scenario goes in the filename.
end note

|#EAF3EC|<color:#1F3556>SKILL CORE  ·  offering-agnostic</color>|
fork
  #E3F0E7:**write_pricing_form.py**
  <size:11>Pricing_Form_scenario.xlsx</size>;
fork again
  #E3F0E7:**write_deck.py**
  <size:11>Proposal_Deck_scenario.pptx</size>;
end fork

|#F4F7FA|<color:#1F3556>SOLUTION SHAPER</color>|
#F2F5F8:Review the artefacts
<size:11>every figure traceable to the RFP, the user, or a flagged default</size>;

if (Approved?) then (**yes**)
  #F2F5F8:Hand to **DO-2 Proposal Writer**
  for the client submission;
  stop
else (no)
  #F2F5F8:Revise inputs or
  service configuration;
  stop
endif

legend right
|= |= Notation |
|<#F2F5F8>            | Human task — Solution Shaper |
|<#DCE7EF>            | AI agent task — GP-20 skill |
|<#E3F0E7>            | Deterministic tool — skill core |
|<#EDE0EE>            | Offering model — pluggable pack |
|<#FDF3E4>            | Decision · architect's observation |
<size:10>Illustrative model — synthetic rates, not NSC pricing.</size>
endlegend

@enduml
